The objective function is to minimize the total walking distance, which is the sum of the Euclidean distances between all pairs of villages multiplied by the corresponding number of elementary school students. The constraints ensure that only two schools can be built.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the optimal solution (if found). It prints the minimum total walking distance and the villages where the schools should be built.

