Then, the script adds constraints, including each train choosing only one approach track, each approach track being chosen by only one train, approach track conflict, minimum dwell time, and safe interval between trains.

Finally, the script solves the model and outputs the results, including which approach track each train chooses.

Note that this script assumes that the objective function is to maximize the speed of trains. If other optimization objectives need to be considered, the objective function and constraints can be modified accordingly.
