### Non-negativity Constraints:
- \(x_{ij} \geq 0, \forall i, j\)
   - This ensures that the number of hours allocated to each component in each workshop is non-negative.

Using this model, we can apply linear programming techniques to find the optimal allocation of hours to each component in each workshop, maximizing the number of completed products while satisfying the production capacity constraints of each workshop. This will provide the production manager with an optimal production plan.

